  "term": "Cohen’s d",
  "definition": "Cohen’s d is a standardized effect size for the difference between means. It expresses how large a mean difference is relative to the standardizer chosen for that difference, helping researchers compare results and use them in cumulative research such as power analysis and meta-analysis.",
